# tier: original-diagnostic
# oracle: independent-derivation
# scenario: demo-lamp-tone-idle
# profile: intv-2609-ntsc-family-p1
# frame: 1 F-S1
# frame: 6 F-S1
# frame: 12 F-S1
# program: fixtures/FX-demo-lamp-tone-1/lamp-tone.listing.txt (ivs-demo-lamp-tone-1), entered through the
#   project boot stub contract 2 (boot-stub-2: cartridge reset entry 5000, interrupt entry 5004), with
#   the zero graphics ROM and no EXEC image
#
# Predicate of ivs-demo-lamp-tone-1 with no controller input (plan 07-07, D-23, D-22, A-02, A-05, A-16;
# the tier is original-diagnostic because the scenario has no input line by design, the shape lint of the
# playable tier does not apply): the guest words at the one bound (marker 03C5, the frame counter 000D,
# both ports at the idle byte FF with no change, no pending amplitude), the idle picture F-S1 in
# frames 1, 6 and 12, frame 0 not displayed, the PSG write log with the six init records only, and
# silence, all derived by hand in docs/video/demo-lamp-tone-1-derivation.md (sections (c) to (f); the
# frame literal data/video/frames/F-S1.frame with its sha256-text key) BEFORE the program, its listing,
# the scenario or any run existed (oracle commit 4e0febef675c2e81fe38d6c0caf353625218b1eb), and copied here line for line from
# the committed idle block. It was not generated by, read back from or edited to match the core or a run.
# The author of this derivation also wrote the literals, the STIC and PSG rules, the program and the core,
# so all of them can share one misreading of a source; agreement among them is not independent evidence
# about hardware.
# Excluded on purpose: machine time (printed in the report, never asserted), all CPU registers, R7 and
# the flags (C40, C45, C56), the stack word [0340] (C68), the exact duration of the interrupt service
# routine and the re-arm delay, the tick of a log record, and the tone phase (the audio is silent at
# every asserted tick).
# Body: one assert per clause in the runner's scenario grammar, hex upper case, exact compare, evaluated
# at the end of the step above it, in the order of data/scenarios/demo-lamp-tone-idle.ivss
# (golden-expect-drift). The step line below is a comment.
# step: run-to 806568 ticks
assert halted == no
assert mem 02F0 == 03C5
assert mem 02F1 == 000D
assert mem 02F2 == 00FF
assert mem 02F3 == 0000
assert mem 02F4 == 00FF
assert mem 02F5 == 0000
assert mem 02F6 == 0000
assert mem 02F7 == 0000
assert frame 0 displayed == no
assert frame 1 displayed == yes
assert frame 12 displayed == yes
assert frame 1 hash == 269b8753dd3b8e011b3fc674e071664433ae997b5f05a8227f8569eb3a1e8e70
assert frame 6 hash == 269b8753dd3b8e011b3fc674e071664433ae997b5f05a8227f8569eb3a1e8e70
